# status-online-stats - the status message, every stat known
#
# Written by hand from the observer firmware's source, agessaman/MeshCore observer-firmware @ d664d89df66bdacc1319900a2e2d152fa31b9dc9.
#   status, timestamp, origin, origin_id, model, firmware_version, radio, client_version, repeat, stats
#                MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:206-216 in that order; repeat only when given (:214-216)
#   model        examples/simple_repeater/MyMesh.cpp:1232  MainBoard::getManufacturerName(): "Heltec V3" (variants/heltec_v3/HeltecV3Board.h:68-70 at the pin)
#   radio        MQTTBridge.cpp:4061-4062  "%.6f,%.1f,%d,%d" of NodePrefs freq (float), bw (float), sf, cr: 869.618 as a float is 869.617981
#   client_version  MQTTBridge.cpp:5117-5123  "meshcore/" + firmware_version
#   repeat       MQTTBridge.cpp:4104  "off" when forwarding is disabled, which for an exit node it always is
#   stats        MQTTPayloadBuilder.cpp:218-254  the object only when a value is known; each field only when known
#                (>= 0; noise_floor > -999; connect_failures and slots_breaker > 0), in the source's order
# Every stat the observer firmware publishes for a board with a battery reading, a dispatcher and a radio (MQTTBridge.cpp:4068-4095);
# mqtt_connect_failures and mqtt_slots_breaker are 0 and therefore left out (:248-253); mqtt_outage_secs is -1 (none timed) and left out (:245-247).
